  "issue": {
    "body": "### Discussed in https://github.com/encode/starlette/discussions/1577\r\n\r\n<div type='discussions-op-text'>\r\n\r\n<sup>Originally posted by **vbsd** April  7, 2022</sup>\r\nIt seems that there is a mistake in starlette's WebSocket [status code list](https://github.com/encode/starlette/blob/0.19.0/starlette/status.py#L83).\r\n\r\nStatus code 1005 has the name `1005_ABNORMAL_CLOSURE` and 1006 is missing altogether. However, [Mozilla MDN docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CloseEvent/code) indicate that 1005 actually means \"no status received\". It is status code 1006 that means \"abnormal closure\".\r\n\r\nIt looks like what should have been\r\n```\r\nWS_1005_NO_STATUS_RECEIVED = 1005\r\nWS_1006_ABNORMAL_CLOSURE = 1006\r\n```\r\ngot mashed together and became just one line:\r\n```\r\nWS_1006_NO_STATUS_RECEIVED = 1005\r\n```\r\n\r\nMaking starlette backwards-incompatible over this wouldn't make much sense, but it seems reasonable to at least add the two correct lines and document `WS_1005_ABNORMAL_CLOSURE` as deprecated/wrong.</div>",
    "body_last_edited_at": null,
    "closed_at": "2022-04-22T04:55:11Z",
    "created_at": "2022-04-07T14:37:36Z",
